rld he has over 250 billion dollars  stockpiled from huge wins with tesla and  spacex so it wouldn't be crazy to say  that he's motivated by money twitter's  value as a company has been stagnant for  years now the stock price really hasn't  moved much over the last nine years but  during that time elon has increased  tesla's share price by more than 30x so  if elon could turn twitter into a  high-growth tech stock certainly he  could make a lot of money right well  it's not quite that simple see at 30  billion dollars in market cap twitter is  still a pretty small company at least by  elon's standards buying the entire  company would cost him around 10 of his  net worth if he then doubles the value  of twitter by improving the service he's  only 10 richer he would need to  completely reinvent the company in order  to make a meaningful profit and he has  way better opportunities in front of him  with spacex and tesla if he can just  deliver the cyber truck a little bit  earlier than expected he'll probably  increase his net worth by more than he  ever could by turning twitter around  it's also surprisingly difficult to buy  100 of the twitter shares even for elon  sure he's worth 250 billion on paper but  he can't convert all of that to cash  overnight he did sell 16 billion dollars  of tesla stock last year but he'd need  even more money to cover the full 30  billion required to buy twitter outright  he could go find a partner to help fund  the purchase but that might be tricky  because then he would have to give up  some control and banks aren't likely to  lend him enough money to do a full  buyout most banks capped their lending  at six times earnings but twitter trades  at 60 times earnings so debt could  really only cover 10 of the sticker  price now that elon has made an offer to  take twitter private lots of people are  speculating how he'll pull together the  money he needs to get it done but elon's  a resourceful guy and even if he has to  take out a massive loan against his  tesla shares he'll do it at the end of  the day this battle is about more than  money to him so we can rule out pure  profit as the main motivation here it's  just too complicated and wouldn't make a  significant impact on elon's total net  worth but maybe it's just a flex  billionaires love to buy fancy things  and what's fancier than owning an app  that 200 million people use around the  world elon has said that he wants to get  rid of his material possessions perhaps  owning twitter would give him more clout  than competing with bezos to build the  world's largest yacht i mean jeff bezos  and elon musk have a long history  together blue origin and spacex are  constantly duking it out to reach new  milestones and win splashy headlines and  jeff bezos did buy the washington post  in 2013 for 250 million dollars so maybe  elon wants to one-up jeff in the media  world and show him who's boss  twitter might cost a hundred times more  money than an old newspaper company but  it certainly has a bigger impact there  are two main ways to look at the value  of twitter you can look at it like a  business or you can look at its impact  on the world for most companies these  two metrics are usually pretty closely  aligned but not for twitter major news  breaks first on twitter journalists  celebrities billionaires and even tech  youtubers hang out there but as a  business twitter has been struggling for  years the company is so behind on  monetization that mark zuckerberg once  said it's as if they drove a clown car  into a gold mine and fell in twitter's  impact on the world is unquestionable  though so owning it would be the perfect  gift for the man who has everything  but the twitter board of directors is  already fighting back against elon's  buyout bid even though this story is a  big surprise twitter already has a set  of defenses in place that could make it  extremely difficult for elon to win this  is because twitter's corporate bylaws  are filled 