nd buy  the entire company he's planning to pay  43 billion dollars to acquire twitter  and take it private this is extremely  risky but could unlock big opportunities  elon is a massive talent magnet for the  world's top engineers and with him at  the helm lots of people want to go work  at twitter even though elon is only  offering a modest 20 premium to the  current share price he's already pumped  the stock 30  just by buying a small stake he  basically turned twitter into a meme  stock overnight and if the board  declines his offer he'll sell his shares  and the market will likely react harshly  twitter gets a ton of traffic every day  but their monetization strategy just  doesn't match the customer base that  they serve changing twitter's business  model would be impossible while they are  a public company but if elon succeeds in  taking the company private we could see  things change pretty dramatically  billionaires can buy lots of things that  average people can't yachts space  companies and even fine art at least  that was the case until channel sponsor  masterworks.org came along and unlocked  fine art investing typically you have to  be extremely wealthy to build a real  portfolio of fine art but masterworks  changes that by allowing you to invest  in world famous artworks from banksy  monet and other iconic artists for just  a fraction of what these pieces  typically cost this is important because  contemporary art prices outpace the s p  500 total return by 164 percent from  1995 to 2021. the entire category has  historically required millions of  dollars to access but masterworks has a  secondary market where you can trade  shares in fine art just like buying a  stock on a trading app getting set up  with masterworks is extremely easy you  just create an account on their site  browse their artwork and then start  diversifying your portfolio with one of  the most stable assets around i like  masterworks because it unlocks an  entirely new market and it